I wrote 21 new robot cases and they all pass the offline format check. Nobody has run them. The Excel checks can't be robot cases, so they are a Codex look brief instead.

1. **Grade mismatch window (B-057, #1873):** 8 cases, N33a to N33h, each with a twin that must fail, plus the switch-off control N33s. Example: two pits 4.1 m apart, Set my own 1 in 100, type 19.45 upstream, CE fills 19.40, Draw, and no window opens. N33e and N33f are written to fail on the first version of the fix and pass on the C-78 one.
2. **Cancelling that window (#1858):** the robot *can* press its Cancel button (only "Use" and "Keep" are blocked). So N33_grade_mismatch_x presses Cancel and checks that nothing is drawn and the "cancelled" line prints. Its switch-off control checks the old two-button window comes back.
3. **Excel export (#1871):** the robot may not press any "Export" button and cannot fill in a Save box. Robot cases N41x_excel_on/off would only ever stop at the first step, so I wrote Codex look K1 in their place. K1 also opens the saved file in Excel.
4. **Pit copied onto a pit (#1867):** unchanged, so run the existing cases. The "N36/C36" names in the brief were working titles for N70/C70. The case actually called N36 is a different bug.
5. **Start-up smoke (N91):** checks Civil, Structural and Manager all load at the installed version and CDCHECK runs. It can't read the ribbon tabs or the "Started" log line.
6. **On screen versus log or file:** every case header and the K1 brief say which is which, and so does the report.
   - **On screen (needs a Codex look):** the Grade mismatch window, the About window, the ribbon, the Pit Schedule status line, the save boxes and the workbook in Excel.
   - **Log or file only:** IL levels, object counts, command-line and log lines, and the saved file's sheet names.
7. **A possible real nuisance, from reading the code only:** if New Pipe opens with the last pipe's levels in it and you choose Set my own, typing a new upstream level carries the old fall across. Example: last levels 19.00 / 18.50, you type 19.45, CE fills 18.95 rather than 19.40. The cases clear the upstream box first to get around it. I didn't add it to the bug carpark because my limits allowed only these files, so the desk should decide.

None of the cases use mouse clicks.

**Validate result:** `24 file(s) checked, 0 invalid` (my 21 plus the 3 existing N90 files).

